1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,600
So we built Eyes. Cameras that don't just watch. They act.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:14,600
AttackNet, our own model, reads body language and flags an attack as it happens. Ninety-two percent accurate on footage it's never seen.

3
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:24,600
The alert spreads across our own mesh, a hundred and thirty nodes from police to MARTA buses, in seconds, even when the internet is down.

4
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:36,600
Then AI agents take over, right in iMessage. One live card, updated in place. Dispatch pages the nearest units, and when an officer replies 'on my way', it turns green.

5
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:45,600
Everyone nearby gets a warning and a safe spot. Need help? EMS is paged, and Eyes guides you until they arrive.

6
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:55,600
Under the hood: a 1.9-million-parameter transformer trained on an NVIDIA GPU, an offline-first mesh, and Gemini agents on Photon. Live today.

7
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:59,600
Eyes. Cameras that watch. Eyes that act.
